cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CSF-Bench: Causal Self-Forecasting Lab"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ortiz
    given-names: Jacob
    alias: agentjakey
repository-code: "https://github.com/agentjakey/causal-self-forecasting"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark testing whether language models can make precommitted, calibrated
  predictions about how their outputs change under blinded causal interventions on their
  internal states. Forecasts are committed with a salted hash before an intervention is
  selected, then scored against the measured effect. Includes same-prompt state-swap controls,
  norm-matched random directions, and a held-out intervention mechanism.
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - ai-safety
  - causal-intervention
  - benchmark
  - language-models
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-07-15"
